\[
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{3}}\cdot \frac{\sqrt{4}}{\sqrt{5}}\cdot \frac{\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{7}}
=
\frac{\sqrt{2\cdot 4\cdot 6}}{\sqrt{3\cdot 5\cdot 7}}
=
\frac{\sqrt{48}}{\sqrt{105}}
\]

Simplify \(\sqrt{48}=4\sqrt{3}\):

\[
\frac{4\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{105}}
\]

Rationalize the denominator by multiplying numerator and denominator by \(\sqrt{105}\):

\[
\frac{4\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{105}}\cdot \frac{\sqrt{105}}{\sqrt{105}}
=
\frac{4\sqrt{315}}{105}
\]

Since \(\sqrt{315}=\sqrt{9\cdot 35}=3\sqrt{35}\),

\[
\frac{4\cdot 3\sqrt{35}}{105}
=
\frac{12\sqrt{35}}{105}
=
\frac{4\sqrt{35}}{35}
\]

The answer is \(\frac{4\sqrt{35}}{35}\).
